{"additionalPlain":"Additional Information\nTrueTandem is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace and affords equal opportunity to all qualified applicants for all positions without regard to protected veteran status, qualified individuals with disabilities and all individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age or any other status protected under local, state or federal laws.  \n\nEqual Opportunity Employer - Minorities/Females/Disabled/Veterans\n\n","additional":"<div>Additional Information</div><div>TrueTandem is an equal opportunity employer, committed to diversity and inclusion in the workplace and affords equal opportunity to all qualified applicants for all positions without regard to protected veteran status, qualified individuals with disabilities and all individuals without regard to race, color, religion, sex, sexual orientation, gender identity, national origin, age or any other status protected under local, state or federal laws.  </div><div><br></div><div>Equal Opportunity Employer - Minorities/Females/Disabled/Veterans</div><div><br></div>","categories":{"commitment":"Full time","location":"Remote","team":"All","allLocations":["Remote"]},"createdAt":1787837121442,"descriptionPlain":"Company Description\nTrueTandem's mission is to be a trusted information technology solutions provider, committed to the success of our customers, communities and employees. To enable this mission, we listen to our customers’ needs, empower our dedicated and talented employees, envision success together, and deliver innovative cost-effective solutions. For our customers, we aim to deliver more power to meet their business outcomes through technology implementation, integration, optimization and customization. We enable some of the most well-known companies, nonprofits and federal agencies in the United States to intelligently plan and develop their applications, modernize their infrastructure and manage their data.\n\n\nThis position requires exceptional leadership, stakeholder engagement, and federal program delivery experience. You will guide cross-functional teams through project initiation, requirements development, architecture planning, Agile delivery, testing, security compliance, deployment, training, and transition to operations.\n\nThe Project manager will serve as the primary delivery lead across program management, client engagement, and solution execution, overseeing contractual deliverables, Agile teams, EPLC governance activities, SA&A support, and ATO readiness while managing scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder expectations.\nRole and Responsibilities:\nLeads the planning, execution, and successful delivery of the portal program, ensuring alignment with contract requirements, mission objectives, and stakeholder expectations.\nManages program scope, schedule, budget, resources, risks, and dependencies across all phases of the software development lifecycle, from initiation through deployment and closeout.\nServes as the primary point of contact for stakeholders, facilitating governance reviews, status reporting, executive briefings, and customer engagement activities.\nDrives Agile delivery efforts by leading cross-functional teams of business analysts, architects, developers, testers, security specialists, and trainers to deliver high-quality solutions\nEnsures compliance with federal security, privacy, accessibility, and governance requirements, including FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, Section 508, EPLC, and Authority to Operate (ATO) activities.\nDevelops and maintains program management artifacts, monitors performance metrics, and oversees knowledge transfer, training, and operational readiness activities to support long-term program success\n \nRequired Skills\n8+ years of project management experience supporting Federal Government IT projects.\n5+ years of experience delivering software development, application modernization, or digital transformation projects.\nDemonstrated experience managing Agile software development projects using Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies.\nExperience supporting Microsoft-based solutions, including Azure, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, or comparable enterprise technologies.\nStrong understanding of FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, and Authority to Operate (ATO) processes.\nProven ability to manage project scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder communications.\nPMP Certification required\nBachelor's Degree\nUS Citizen and active Public Trust clearance\nPreferred Skills\nExperience supporting CDC, NIOSH, HHS, or other Federal Government agencies.\nExperience managing projects involving citizen-facing portals, case management solutions, or healthcare/public health systems.\nExperience supporting HHS Enterprise Performance Life Cycle (EPLC) processes.\nAgile certification (Scrum Master, PMI-ACP, SAFe, or equivalent).\n \n","description":"<div>Company Description</div><div>TrueTandem's mission is to be a trusted information technology solutions provider, committed to the success of our customers, communities and employees. To enable this mission, we listen to our customers’ needs, empower our dedicated and talented employees, envision success together, and deliver innovative cost-effective solutions. For our customers, we aim to deliver more power to meet their business outcomes through technology implementation, integration, optimization and customization. We enable some of the most well-known companies, nonprofits and federal agencies in the United States to intelligently plan and develop their applications, modernize their infrastructure and manage their data.</div><div><br></div><div>\n<p>This position requires exceptional leadership, stakeholder engagement, and federal program delivery experience. You will guide cross-functional teams through project initiation, requirements development, architecture planning, Agile delivery, testing, security compliance, deployment, training, and transition to operations.<br><br>The Project manager will serve as the primary delivery lead across program management, client engagement, and solution execution, overseeing contractual deliverables, Agile teams, EPLC governance activities, SA&amp;A support, and ATO readiness while managing scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder expectations.</p>\n<p>Role and Responsibilities:</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>Leads the planning, execution, and successful delivery of the portal program, ensuring alignment with contract requirements, mission objectives, and stakeholder expectations.</li>\n<li>Manages program scope, schedule, budget, resources, risks, and dependencies across all phases of the software development lifecycle, from initiation through deployment and closeout.</li>\n<li>Serves as the primary point of contact for stakeholders, facilitating governance reviews, status reporting, executive briefings, and customer engagement activities.</li>\n<li>Drives Agile delivery efforts by leading cross-functional teams of business analysts, architects, developers, testers, security specialists, and trainers to deliver high-quality solutions</li>\n<li>Ensures compliance with federal security, privacy, accessibility, and governance requirements, including FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, Section 508, EPLC, and Authority to Operate (ATO) activities.</li>\n<li>Develops and maintains program management artifacts, monitors performance metrics, and oversees knowledge transfer, training, and operational readiness activities to support long-term program success</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Required Skills</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>8+ years of project management experience supporting Federal Government IT projects.</li>\n<li>5+ years of experience delivering software development, application modernization, or digital transformation projects.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated experience managing Agile software development projects using Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies.</li>\n<li>Experience supporting Microsoft-based solutions, including Azure, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, or comparable enterprise technologies.</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, and Authority to Operate (ATO) processes.</li>\n<li>Proven ability to manage project scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder communications.</li>\n<li>PMP Certification required</li>\n<li>Bachelor's Degree</li>\n<li>US Citizen and active Public Trust clearance</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Preferred Skills</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>Experience supporting CDC, NIOSH, HHS, or other Federal Government agencies.</li>\n<li>Experience managing projects involving citizen-facing portals, case management solutions, or healthcare/public health systems.</li>\n<li>Experience supporting HHS Enterprise Performance Life Cycle (EPLC) processes.</li>\n<li>Agile certification (Scrum Master, PMI-ACP, SAFe, or equivalent).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</div>","id":"2e56e4d7-b3b5-4f98-bab1-d4eeb38cb2ec","lists":[],"salaryRange":{"min":145000,"max":157000,"currency":"USD","interval":"per-year-salary"},"salaryDescription":"<div>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: black;\">The above salary range represents a general guideline; however, TrueTandem considers several factors when determining base salary offers such as the scope and responsibilities of the position and the candidate's experience, education, skills and current market conditions.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: black;\">In addition, TrueTandem provides a variety of benefits including health insurance coverage, dental and vision plans, life and disability insurance, company paid holidays and paid time off (PTO). Our retirement plan offers a variety of investment options to build toward your retirement.</span></p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</p>\n<p style=\"margin: 0in; font-size: 12pt; font-family: Aptos, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-size: 11pt; color: black;\">U.S. Citizenship is required for all positions with a government clearance and certain other restricted positions.</span></p>\n</div>","salaryDescriptionPlain":"The above salary range represents a general guideline; however, TrueTandem considers several factors when determining base salary offers such as the scope and responsibilities of the position and the candidate's experience, education, skills and current market conditions.\n \nIn addition, TrueTandem provides a variety of benefits including health insurance coverage, dental and vision plans, life and disability insurance, company paid holidays and paid time off (PTO). Our retirement plan offers a variety of investment options to build toward your retirement.\n \n \nU.S. Citizenship is required for all positions with a government clearance and certain other restricted positions.\n","text":"Project Manager","country":"US","workplaceType":"remote","opening":"<div>Company Description</div><div>TrueTandem's mission is to be a trusted information technology solutions provider, committed to the success of our customers, communities and employees. To enable this mission, we listen to our customers’ needs, empower our dedicated and talented employees, envision success together, and deliver innovative cost-effective solutions. For our customers, we aim to deliver more power to meet their business outcomes through technology implementation, integration, optimization and customization. We enable some of the most well-known companies, nonprofits and federal agencies in the United States to intelligently plan and develop their applications, modernize their infrastructure and manage their data.</div>","openingPlain":"Company Description\nTrueTandem's mission is to be a trusted information technology solutions provider, committed to the success of our customers, communities and employees. To enable this mission, we listen to our customers’ needs, empower our dedicated and talented employees, envision success together, and deliver innovative cost-effective solutions. For our customers, we aim to deliver more power to meet their business outcomes through technology implementation, integration, optimization and customization. We enable some of the most well-known companies, nonprofits and federal agencies in the United States to intelligently plan and develop their applications, modernize their infrastructure and manage their data.\n","descriptionBody":"<div>\n<p>This position requires exceptional leadership, stakeholder engagement, and federal program delivery experience. You will guide cross-functional teams through project initiation, requirements development, architecture planning, Agile delivery, testing, security compliance, deployment, training, and transition to operations.<br><br>The Project manager will serve as the primary delivery lead across program management, client engagement, and solution execution, overseeing contractual deliverables, Agile teams, EPLC governance activities, SA&amp;A support, and ATO readiness while managing scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder expectations.</p>\n<p>Role and Responsibilities:</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>Leads the planning, execution, and successful delivery of the portal program, ensuring alignment with contract requirements, mission objectives, and stakeholder expectations.</li>\n<li>Manages program scope, schedule, budget, resources, risks, and dependencies across all phases of the software development lifecycle, from initiation through deployment and closeout.</li>\n<li>Serves as the primary point of contact for stakeholders, facilitating governance reviews, status reporting, executive briefings, and customer engagement activities.</li>\n<li>Drives Agile delivery efforts by leading cross-functional teams of business analysts, architects, developers, testers, security specialists, and trainers to deliver high-quality solutions</li>\n<li>Ensures compliance with federal security, privacy, accessibility, and governance requirements, including FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, Section 508, EPLC, and Authority to Operate (ATO) activities.</li>\n<li>Develops and maintains program management artifacts, monitors performance metrics, and oversees knowledge transfer, training, and operational readiness activities to support long-term program success</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<p>Required Skills</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>8+ years of project management experience supporting Federal Government IT projects.</li>\n<li>5+ years of experience delivering software development, application modernization, or digital transformation projects.</li>\n<li>Demonstrated experience managing Agile software development projects using Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies.</li>\n<li>Experience supporting Microsoft-based solutions, including Azure, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, or comparable enterprise technologies.</li>\n<li>Strong understanding of FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, and Authority to Operate (ATO) processes.</li>\n<li>Proven ability to manage project scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder communications.</li>\n<li>PMP Certification required</li>\n<li>Bachelor's Degree</li>\n<li>US Citizen and active Public Trust clearance</li>\n</ul>\n<p>Preferred Skills</p>\n<ul type=\"disc\">\n<li>Experience supporting CDC, NIOSH, HHS, or other Federal Government agencies.</li>\n<li>Experience managing projects involving citizen-facing portals, case management solutions, or healthcare/public health systems.</li>\n<li>Experience supporting HHS Enterprise Performance Life Cycle (EPLC) processes.</li>\n<li>Agile certification (Scrum Master, PMI-ACP, SAFe, or equivalent).</li>\n</ul>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n</div>","descriptionBodyPlain":"This position requires exceptional leadership, stakeholder engagement, and federal program delivery experience. You will guide cross-functional teams through project initiation, requirements development, architecture planning, Agile delivery, testing, security compliance, deployment, training, and transition to operations.\n\nThe Project manager will serve as the primary delivery lead across program management, client engagement, and solution execution, overseeing contractual deliverables, Agile teams, EPLC governance activities, SA&A support, and ATO readiness while managing scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder expectations.\nRole and Responsibilities:\nLeads the planning, execution, and successful delivery of the portal program, ensuring alignment with contract requirements, mission objectives, and stakeholder expectations.\nManages program scope, schedule, budget, resources, risks, and dependencies across all phases of the software development lifecycle, from initiation through deployment and closeout.\nServes as the primary point of contact for stakeholders, facilitating governance reviews, status reporting, executive briefings, and customer engagement activities.\nDrives Agile delivery efforts by leading cross-functional teams of business analysts, architects, developers, testers, security specialists, and trainers to deliver high-quality solutions\nEnsures compliance with federal security, privacy, accessibility, and governance requirements, including FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, Section 508, EPLC, and Authority to Operate (ATO) activities.\nDevelops and maintains program management artifacts, monitors performance metrics, and oversees knowledge transfer, training, and operational readiness activities to support long-term program success\n \nRequired Skills\n8+ years of project management experience supporting Federal Government IT projects.\n5+ years of experience delivering software development, application modernization, or digital transformation projects.\nDemonstrated experience managing Agile software development projects using Scrum, Kanban, or hybrid methodologies.\nExperience supporting Microsoft-based solutions, including Azure, Power Platform, Dynamics 365, or comparable enterprise technologies.\nStrong understanding of FISMA, FedRAMP, NIST, and Authority to Operate (ATO) processes.\nProven ability to manage project scope, schedule, budget, risks, and stakeholder communications.\nPMP Certification required\nBachelor's Degree\nUS Citizen and active Public Trust clearance\nPreferred Skills\nExperience supporting CDC, NIOSH, HHS, or other Federal Government agencies.\nExperience managing projects involving citizen-facing portals, case management solutions, or healthcare/public health systems.\nExperience supporting HHS Enterprise Performance Life Cycle (EPLC) processes.\nAgile certification (Scrum Master, PMI-ACP, SAFe, or equivalent).\n \n","hostedUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/truetandem/2e56e4d7-b3b5-4f98-bab1-d4eeb38cb2ec","applyUrl":"https://jobs.lever.co/truetandem/2e56e4d7-b3b5-4f98-bab1-d4eeb38cb2ec/apply"}